# Two Twinflame Travelers each make a triggered ability of another Elemental Bot1 controls trigger an additional time
# (CR 603.2d): Flickerwisp's "When Flickerwisp enters, exile another target permanent ..." triggers three times. Each
# triggering chooses its own target as it goes on the stack (CR 603.3d): the first and second Bot2's Mox Jet, the third
# Bot2's Island. The last one put on the stack resolves first and exiles the Island, the next exiles the Mox, and the
# first, whose target has left the battlefield, is removed as it tries to resolve (CR 608.2b). Only the two that resolved
# set up a return (a delayed triggered ability is no ability of Flickerwisp, so the Travelers do not double it either):
# the Mox and the Island come back at the beginning of the end step.
# Mana: turn 1 Mox Ruby and Black Lotus (UUU) pay the first Travelers; turn 3 the Volcanic Island, Plateau, Ruby and Pearl
# the second; turn 5 Plains, Pearl and Ruby pay Flickerwisp's {1}{W}{W}.

